<task id="061" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Implement §4C rollback semantics — 4-class failure taxonomy + Quarantined state + clear-quarantine audit</title>
    <phase>C Wave C5 — L2 REST + Reconciler</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Task tags include 'l2-controlplane','job-handler','auth'; implements FR-24 rollback semantics; a bug here strands runs OR silently retries a Quarantine-required failure. Audit-log obligation makes this security-adjacent.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>4-class taxonomy → state transition table encoded in code + Cosmos state store transitions + audit-log wiring. Requires careful reasoning through each class's semantics but scoped. Step 3.5.5b sonnet @ xhigh justified per complex-brownfield criteria.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>057, 058</deps>
    <tags>l2-controlplane, job-handler, auth, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Implement the §4C rollback semantics per spec.md FR-24 + design.md §4C. Classify handler failures into 4 classes: (1) Resumable — retry after external precondition; (2) Retryable-with-cleanup — re-run handler; own idempotency handles partial write; (3) Quarantine-required — Cosmos Quarantined state blocks new runs against same customerId until operator explicitly clears via POST /api/runs/{id}/clear-quarantine (audit-logged); (4) Successful-but-drifted — H13 detects; operator re-runs affected phases with resumeFromPhase param. Each class round-trips through Cosmos state correctly per the §4C state-transition table. POST /api/runs/{id}/clear-quarantine requires a reason and audit-logs to App Insights.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in state-machine encoding, Cosmos DB state transitions, App Insights audit event patterns, and mapping domain-level failure taxonomy to enum + policy code. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>Failure classification is encoded as an enum FailureClass { Resumable, RetryableWithCleanup, QuarantineRequired, SuccessfulButDrifted } in src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Rollback/**. Reconciler + handlers translate exceptions/results into a FailureClass via a policy component. Cosmos state transitions per class match the §4C state-transition table. POST /api/runs/{id}/clear-quarantine (implemented in task 057) is wired to a QuarantineClearService that verifies the run is in Quarantined state, transitions it to Failed (post-quarantine), and audit-logs to App Insights with actor tid + reason. Unit + integration tests cover each class's state transition + clear-quarantine happy/negative paths.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Per spec.md FR-24 + design.md §4C: prior generations of provisioning had no explicit failure taxonomy — every failure was "retry or manual fix." v3.2 added the 4-class taxonomy to make failure handling deterministic and to give operators a reversible "quarantine cleared" mechanism for the class that CANNOT auto-recover (e.g., corrupted partial-write). Quarantined state blocks new runs against the same customerId until explicitly cleared.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Rollback/FailureClass.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Rollback/IFailureClassifier.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Rollback/FailureClassifier.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Rollback/QuarantineClearService.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Rollback/RollbackTransitions.Tests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Reconciler/StateReconcilerService.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Api/RunsEndpoints.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="057" status="pending">POST /api/runs/{id}/clear-quarantine endpoint shape (invokes QuarantineClearService)</dependency>
      <dependency task="058" status="pending">Reconciler dispatch loop — translates handler outcomes into FailureClass transitions</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec.md FR-24">SCOPE: 4-class taxonomy exactly per §4C — no additional classes; no merging of classes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md FR-24">SCOPE: Quarantined runs block NEW runs against the same customerId (integrate with task 059 I5 concurrency guard — a customer with a Quarantined active run cannot start a new run until cleared).</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md FR-24">SCOPE: clear-quarantine REQUIRES a reason parameter and MUST audit-log actor tid + reason + before/after state to App Insights (TelemetryClient.TrackEvent("QuarantineCleared", ...)).</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md FR-24">SCOPE: Successful-but-drifted class — H13 detects; the reclassification path allows operator to invoke POST /api/runs/{id}/resume with a resumeFromPhase parameter targeting the drifted phase; do NOT auto-retry.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-036">SCOPE: Resumable + Retryable-with-cleanup classes trigger normal re-enqueue via Service Bus + 3-level-idempotent handler stack; no bespoke retry loop.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: FailureClass is an ENUM (not a string); the reconciler-to-Cosmos translation is a switch with an exhaustive-guard so a new class MUST be handled explicitly at compile time.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: Terminal-state ReleaseAsync (task 059) does NOT fire on QuarantineRequired — the customer stays blocked until clear-quarantine explicitly runs.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>4-class failure taxonomy with Cosmos state transitions and audit-logged clear-quarantine</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-004-job-contract.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-036-background-job-infrastructure.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/jobs.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md</file>
