  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a handler failure classified Resumable, when the reconciler processes the outcome, then Cosmos state transitions per §4C Resumable row (status stays Running / WaitingOnGate with retry-schedule metadata).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a handler failure classified Retryable-with-cleanup, when the reconciler processes the outcome, then the handler is re-enqueued with the same idempotency key and Cosmos state matches §4C row 2.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a handler failure classified Quarantine-required, when the reconciler processes the outcome, then Cosmos state = Quarantined and no re-enqueue is triggered.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a Quarantined run for customer C, when TryAcquireAsync(C, newRunId) is invoked, then result = Conflict with reasonCode = "Quarantined" (integrates with task 059).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a Quarantined run, when POST /api/runs/{id}/clear-quarantine is invoked with reason by Operator, then the state transitions to Failed, CustomerRunGuard is released, and App Insights receives QuarantineCleared with actor tid + reason.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: clear-quarantine without reason returns 400; on a non-Quarantined run returns 409; unauthorized returns 403.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a handler flagged Successful-but-drifted by H13, when the reconciler processes the outcome, then state = Completed with driftDetected = true; operator re-runs affected phases via resume with resumeFromPhase.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build exits 0; dotnet test exits 0; zero analyzer warnings.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Reference: spec.md FR-24 + design.md §4C state-transition table + spec.md ADR Tensions row 1 (ADR-004 Path A at L2 scope).</notes>

